- for every index $$$i \in [1, n - 1]$$$ either $$$b_i = b_{i + 1}$$$ or $$$b_i + 1 = b_{i + 1}$$$.

For example, if $$$a = [1, 2, 1, 2, 3]$$$, then two possible monotonic renumerations of $$$a$$$ are $$$b = [0, 0, 0, 0, 0]$$$ and $$$b = [0, 0, 0, 0, 1]$$$.

