A. Sakurako and Kosuke

Simulate the process: starting from $x=0$, on the $i$-th move if it's Sakurako's turn (odd move) subtract $2i-1$, if it's Kosuke's turn (even move) add $2i-1$, continuing while $-n \le x \le n$. After the loop, check whose turn it was last.

```
def solve:
