E. Sakurako, Kosuke, and the Permutation

Decompose the permutation into cycles. A cycle of length $1$ or $2$ is already simple. For a cycle of length $\ell$, we need $\lfloor (\ell - 1) / 2 \rfloor$ swaps to break it into fixed points and transpositions. Sum this over all cycles.

```cpp
#include<bits/stdc++.h>
