Count the number of '-' characters (call it $\text{dash}$) and '_' characters (call it $\text{under} = n - \text{dash}$). To maximize the number of subsequences equal to "-_-", we want to split the dashes into two halves: $\lfloor \text{dash}/2 \rfloor$ dashes at the beginning, then all underscores, then the remaining $\text{dash} - \lfloor \text{dash}/2 \rfloor$ dashes at the end. The answer is $\lfloor \text{dash}/2 \rfloor \cdot (\text{dash} - \lfloor \text{dash}/2 \rfloor) \cdot \text{under}$.

```cpp
