Consider sequences of operations. The valid sequences alternate between going left (choosing '<' arrows) and going right (choosing '>' arrows). 

For a sequence ending with a '<' arrow at position $i$: we can take any subset of '>' arrows before position $i$ (with positive rewards), then arrow $i$. The optimal prefix contribution from '>' arrows is the sum of positive rewards among '>' arrows seen so far (a running sum of $\max(c_j, 0)$ for '>' arrows). So for each '<' arrow at position $i$, the candidate answer is $\text{sum\_positive\_rights\_before\_i} + c_i$.

By symmetry, we do the same pass from right to left for sequences ending with a '>' arrow.

The answer is the maximum over all candidates and 0.

