Since $a_i \leq 100$, we can iterate over all possible median values $i$ from $1$ to $100$. For a fixed median value $i$, replace each array element with $+1$ if $a_j \geq i$ and $-1$ otherwise. Then element $j$ has median $\geq i$ in some subarray containing $j$ if and only if there exists a subarray where the sum of the $\pm 1$ array is $\geq 0$ (i.e., the median position has a $+1$ value). We want to find, for each position $j$ (as the minimum element position), whether there's a valid subarray achieving median $\geq i$ with minimum $a_j$.

For each $j$, check if $\text{prefmn}[j-1] \leq \text{pref}[j]$ or $\text{pref}[j-1] \leq \text{suffmx}[j]$ (conditions for a subarray containing $j$ having nonnegative prefix sum difference). If so, update the answer with $i - a_j$.

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
